    "case_id": "684",
    "case_summary": "A 26-year-old female was referred for root canal retreatment of the maxillary right second molar (tooth #17) due to spontaneous dull pain during the process of root canal therapy in another stomatological hospital. The patient's medical history was negative.\n\nClinical examination showed:- Tooth sealed with temporary filling material- Tender in response to percussion- No response to cold or electric pulp tests\n\n- Radiological examination:  - Radiopaque filling material visible in coronal third of canal  - Periapical radiolucency present at apex of DB root  - CBCT Findings (0.15mm resolution):  - Axial image revealed C-shaped canal morphology in P root  - Two different canal orifices in coronal third of P canal  - Middle third showed canals joined to form C-shaped ribbon-like pattern  - Sagittal image showed two P canals joined to one foramen in apical part",
